# The 50x receipt beside p6_tree_speed_fast: 24 nodes, at 1x and then at 50x
# in one run (tree.html?nodes=24&seed=7&links=none&gpu=off&physics_speed=1).
# 50x must reach half the lesser of 50 times the page's own 1x and the speed
# its step budget fits at the run's measured tick cost (physics catalog plan,
# ruled 2026-10-06, "Half of the lesser"), so the bar follows the load: under
# load the budget, not the dial, limits 50x. Its control,
# p6_tree_speed_fast_control_capped, plants a cap so 50x owes what 1x owes,
# and must miss the bar.
assert snap ready == true
assert snap physics-speed == 1
assert snap physics-budget-share == 0.5
assert snap physics-budget-margin-us == 200
click role:button Play physics
settle 2
assert snap physics-paused == false
click role:combobox Arrangement
settle 1
click role:option Free (physics alone)
settle 1
click role:button Apply arrangement
settle 1
assert snap layout == free
# Fill the 32-frame effective-speed meter at 1x before marking it.
settle 32
mark-pace one-x
assert snap physics-effective-marked >= 0.001
click role:combobox Speed
settle 1
click role:option 50x
# Replace the meter's 1x frames before testing the selected speed.
settle 32
assert snap physics-speed == 50
timing start speed-fast-control
settle 4
timing stop
log-physics fast-control
log-pace fast-control
assert snap physics-effective-over-bar >= 1
# The period read is at most the 1/60 s cap, the budget at most half of it.
assert snap display-period-ms <= 16.7
assert snap physics-budget-us <= 8333
# Each frame's admitted ticks inside its own budget plus the clock's 100 us
# grain, over every window, as p6_tree_speed_fast.
assert snap pace-gated-frames >= 1
assert snap pace-over-budget-us <= 100
assert snap pace-over-budget-worst-us <= 100
assert snap pace-over-grain-frames == 0
assert snap finite == true
log p6 speed fast control receipt complete
